 "intro_html": "A bowl of rice crowned with small heaps of <b>seasoned vegetables (namul)</b>, beef and a fried egg, mixed together at the table. It's a good way to use leftover <a href=\"bulgogi.html\">bulgogi</a> or <a href=\"dak-bulgogi.html\">dak bulgogi</a>. Every vegetable is cooked in the same steel pan one after another. At the end the pan does what a hot stone bowl (dolsot) does: rice pressed into hot sesame oil forms a <b>crisp golden crust</b>. Gochujang sauce is traditional; a <b>mild soy-sesame sauce</b> is given too. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
